    div
      h6 How to Analyze WeiboScope Search Data
      p
        img(src='/images/weibo3.jpg' width='100%')
      p
        a(href='http://jmsc.hku.hk/2010/02/bio-king-wa-fu/') King-Wa Fu
        |  and 
        a(href='http://jmsc.hku.hk/blogs/ricecooker/') Cedric Sam
        |  at the 
        a(href='http://jmsc.hku.hk/') University of Hong Kong&rsquo;s Journalism and Media Studies Centre
        |  have built a 
        a(href='http://research.jmsc.hku.hk/social/search.py/sinaweibo/#lastpermissiondenied') WeiboScope Search
        |  that sends all of the deleted Weibo posts to a server in Hong Kong and stores them.  However, the data is in JSON format, which looks like this:
        img(src='/images/weibo4.jpg' width='100%')
      p
        | To make sense of the data collected, we need to first clean up the data. I used 
        a(href='http://code.google.com/p/google-refine/') Google refine
        |  to clean up the data by:
      ol
        ol 1) Download + install Google refine
        ol 2) Click on &ldquo;Create Project&rdquo;
        ol 3) Click on &ldquo;Web Addresses (URLs)&rdquo;
      p
        img(src='/images/weibo5.jpg' width='100%')
      ol
        ol
          | 4) Insert link http://research.jmsc.hku.hk/social/sinaweibo/lastpermissiondenied.all.json
        ol 5) Click &ldquo;Next&rdquo;
      p
        img(src='/images/weibo6.jpg' width='100%')
      ol
        ol 6) Highlight the fields you&rsquo;re interested in and left click the mouse.
      p
        img(src='/images/weibo7.jpg' width='100%')
      ol Google refine should automatically put all the fields into columns:
      p
        img(src='/images/weibo81.jpg' width='100%')
      ol
        ol 7) Click &ldquo;Create Project&rdquo;
        ol 8) Click &ldquo;Export&rdquo;
        ol 9) Click &ldquo;Excel&rdquo;
      p
        img(src='/images/weibo10.jpg' width='100%')
      p Now that we have the data formatted, we want to make sense of it.
      p
        | The first project I did was to graph the deleted weibos on a timeline. My classmate 
        a(href='http://www.mit.edu/~eugenewu/') Eugene Wu 
        |  suggested that the best software to visualize the data is 
        a(href='http://www.tableausoftware.com/') Tableau
        | .
      ol
        ol 1) Download + install Tableau
        ol 2) Click on &ldquo;Open Data&rdquo;
        ol 3) Under &ldquo;Connect to Data: In a file&rdquo;, click on &ldquo;Microsoft Excel&rdquo;
        ol 4) When the &ldquo;Excel Workbook Connection&rdquo; window pops up, click &ldquo;Ok&rdquo;
      p
        img(src='/images/weibo11.jpg' width='100%')
      ol
        ol
          | 5) Change the format for the &ldquo;created at&rdquo; and &ldquo;deleted&rdquo; columns from &ldquo;text&rdquo; to &ldquo;Date &amp; time&rdquo; by right clicking the mouse, selecting &ldquo;Change Data Type&rdquo; then &ldquo;Date &amp; time.&rdquo;
      p
        img(src='/images/weibo12.jpg' width='100%')
      ol
        ol
          ol 6) Go to the Dimensions box and drag the &ldquo;deleted&rdquo; data set to &ldquo;Columns&rdquo;
          ol 7) Go to the Measures box and drag the &ldquo;Number of Records&rdquo; data set to &ldquo;Rows&rdquo;
          ol 8) In the &ldquo;Show Me&rdquo; box, select the type of graph you want. Voila!
      div
        img(src='/images/censored_weibo_timeline1.png' width='100%')
      div(style='text-align: right')
        a(href='http://public.tableausoftware.com/views/MASS61finalproject/censoredweibotimeline')
          span(style='font-size: x-small') Powered by Tableau
